---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const title = "Download llmsx — the concept-pack CLI and TUI";
const description =
  "llmsx: a dependency-free CLI, plus an optional Textual TUI, over the concept tree and llms-concept-abstractor concept packs — install from source today, thin skill wrappers for concept-family-explorer and llms-deep-optimizer, no account needed.";

const EXTRAS = [
  ["(none)", "tree, concepts list/show/serve — stdlib only", "no install extra"],
  ["tui", "llmsx tui, llmsx concepts tui — the Textual browsers", "pip install 'llmsx[tui]'"],
  ["skills", "llmsx family <topic>, llmsx optimize <file-or-text>", "pip install 'llmsx[skills]'"],
];

const NOUNS = [
  ["llmsx tree show [root] [--depth N]", "indented concept tree, frontier marked"],
  ["llmsx tree detail <slug>", "one tree node's fields"],
  ["llmsx tree search <query>", "concept + alias substring search"],
  ["llmsx tree frontier [slug]", "concepts named but never researched"],
  ["llmsx tui", "the Textual tree browser"],
  ["llmsx concepts list [--query Q]", "catalog every concept pack — summary, useful_for, related terms"],
  ["llmsx concepts show <slug>", "one pack's summary, facets, related terms, files"],
  ["llmsx concepts serve <slug> [--file F]", "print a pack file to stdout — pipeable"],
  ["llmsx concepts tui", "the Textual concept-pack browser"],
  ["llmsx family <topic>", "one model turn against concept-family-explorer"],
  ["llmsx optimize <file-or-text>", "one model turn against llms-deep-optimizer"],
];
---
<Base title={title} description={description} route="/download/">
  <p>
    <code>llmsx</code> is not hosted yet — there is no account, no key, nothing metered. It is a
    small Python package you run against your own files: the site's generated concept
    tree, or a directory of concept packs built by <a href="/skills/llms-concept-abstractor/">the
    concept abstractor</a> (<code>/lca</code>) or <code>llms-deep-optimizer --family</code>
    (<code>/ldo</code>). The base CLI has zero third-party dependencies; the two Textual
    browsers and the skill wrappers are opt-in extras.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <p>
    Not on PyPI yet — install from source. Requires Python 3.11+.
  </p>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/mithudso/llms-explorer.git
cd llms-explorer/llmsx
pip install .                 # base CLI, no dependencies
pip install '.[tui]'          # + the Textual browsers
pip install '.[skills]'       # + llmsx family / llmsx optimize (needs an Anthropic key)
pip install '.[tui,skills]'   # everything</code></pre>
  <p>
    Or without installing anything: <code>cd llms-explorer/llmsx && python -m llmsx …</code>
    works the same way (see the <a href="https://github.com/mithudso/llms-explorer/tree/main/llmsx">
    package README</a> for the one case where that shadows itself as a namespace package).
  </p>

  <h2>What you get</h2>
  <table class="family-files">
    <tbody>
      {NOUNS.map(([cmd, note]) => (
        <tr>
          <td><code>{cmd}</code></td>
          <td>{note}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Extras</h2>
  <table class="family-files">
    <tbody>
      {EXTRAS.map(([extra, covers, install]) => (
        <tr>
          <td><code>[{extra}]</code></td>
          <td>{covers}</td>
          <td><code>{install}</code></td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Two different "concepts"</h2>
  <p>
    <code>llmsx tui</code> and <code>llmsx concepts tui</code> browse two different data
    models, on purpose. The tree (<code>llmsx tree</code>/<code>llmsx tui</code>) is this
    site's own SEO/research concept tree — see <a href="/family/">this site's llms family</a>
    for what it's built from. Concept packs (<code>llmsx concepts</code>) are
    <code>&lt;slug&gt;.llms/</code> directories the concept-abstractor skill builds around one
    named concept: a <code>manifest.json</code>, a <code>concept-graph.json</code> of related
    terms, and the familiar <code>llms.txt</code>/<code>llms-full.txt</code>/<code>llms-small.txt</code>/<code>llms-facts.txt</code>/<code>llms-vocabulary.txt</code>
    ladder — pointed by default at <code>~/.global-ai-hub/llms-concepts</code>, overridable
    with <code>--data</code> or <code>$LLMSX_CONCEPTS_PATH</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Running a skill from the CLI</h2>
  <p>
    <code>llmsx family</code> and <code>llmsx optimize</code> are thin wrappers over
    <code>llmsx.skills.run_skill</code>: one model turn holding the named skill's own
    instructions as the system prompt, your input as the user turn. Both print a one-line
    disclaimer before the model's output, because it is genuinely not the same thing as
    running <a href="/skills/concept-family-explorer/">concept-family-explorer</a> or
    <a href="/skills/full-suite/">the full suite</a> end to end — those orchestrate multi-pass
    loops, subagent fan-out and concept-tree writes that a single API call does not drive.
    Useful for a quick read on a topic or a file; not a substitute for the loop when you need
    the loop.
  </p>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <p>
    MIT licensed. Source and issues live at
    <a href="https://github.com/mithudso/llms-explorer/tree/main/llmsx">github.com/mithudso/llms-explorer/tree/main/llmsx</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
